c={
'B01':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Same number; retain the pagination wrapper.','ink':'The top figure has a long upper stroke, descending diagonal and crossbar. Both readings identify7; the mspage macro records its isolated position without attributing the hand.'},
'B02':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain the two crossed-word alternatives in their existing order.','ink':'A long run of small bodies precedes a late p-like descender, favouring correspondant. The cancellation crosses the intervening joins, so comprenant remains possible. Neither reader has recovered every letter.'},
'B03':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain l/lambda uncertainty.','ink':'The second tuple component has a tall closed upper loop and a lower rightward foot, favouring l, but a separate left branch/retraced diagonal makes the local form atypical. Gamma and the following membership in Gamma are clear.'},
'B04':{'final':f['B04'].replace(*slash),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Qualify the curved slash after l.','ink':'After the looped l is one long oblique stroke that curves at both ends. Its downward-left slope favours a slash; its curved course also permits a closing parenthesis. It is visibly separate from de and cannot be omitted. The inverse exponent on gamma and the basepoint P are clear.'},
'B05':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain the readable l in the complete product formula.','ink':'Inside the right-hand gamma-prime inverse application, the overwritten character still has the closed upper l loop and a sweeping lower foot, matching the path letters in both input pairs. No distinct alternative letter is isolated. The gamma gamma-prime component is raised and inserted; the primes, inverse and composition circle are clear.'},
'B06':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Quotation serialization only.','ink':'There are two short high strokes before composant and two after fonctions. The specified paired backticks/apostrophes represent them; curly typographic quotation marks are not a different ink reading.'},
'B07':{'final':f['B07'].replace(*left),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Reopen the tiny à/colon form within the underline.','ink':'Before gauche are a short low curved body and a separate upper dark point. They can be the compressed a and accent of à, but do not exclude a colon. The underline extends beneath this sign as well as gauche; the descending g crosses it without cancelling the word.'},
'B09':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain a solid low dot and the a/x fibre-index doubt.','ink':'The mark below/right of l is a compact round dot without star arms. The following colon has two separate points. The first U index has a small loop and rightward/downward return, favouring a over x but remaining retraced. The arrow points right; U-prime-y and three terminal points are visible.'},
'B10':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain the raised lambda_i and displayed two lists.','ink':'The inserted path sign has an open arched top, a long right descending leg and a shorter left branch, unlike the closed upper loops of the page’s l forms. Its small i is separate. The three first sigmas have no high dots; each in the second list has its own dot. The guide joins the path label after chemins.'},
'B11':{'final':f['B11'].replace(*to),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Qualify à/colon after P; retain l’unique and demi-.','ink':'Between P and barred P are two compact dark marks, vertically separated, which allow either a compressed accented à or a colon. The cancelled word has l, apostrophe, low u/n/i bodies, a q descender and final u/e course: l’unique, rather than the different ascenders and length of équateur/hémisphère. Demi- has d, connected e/m/i and a separate end dash. The raised replacement reads celui des.'},
'B12':{'final':f['B12'].replace(*cross),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Retain ens. des pts fixes; broaden the crossed short sign after par.','ink':'The raised replacement begins with low e/n/s bodies followed by a separate stop, then des, the compact p/t/s abbreviation, and fixes with f and crossed x. It does not begin with the deep p and tall terminal t of passant. The old stable/par/la/symétrie bodies remain identifiable through their horizontal strike. Between par and la, a low dark body lies on that strike below a detached short upper mark: à and dotted tau remain possible.'},
'B13':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain cancelled tau-sigma_i and omit unestablished terminal punctuation.','ink':'The old tau has a broad roof and low return; sigma has a looped body and its low i. A strike traverses both. The live formula carries separate high dots over all four letters. Tiny faint flecks beyond the final symétrie are much weaker than the neighbouring ink and do not establish a comma or colon.'},
'B14':{'final':f['B14'].replace(*plan),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Keep au/à unresolved and add the possible segmentation à un.','ink':'The accented initial body and its low continuation are followed by another compact low course before the large strokes of plan. The spacing and joined strokes admit à un as well as the previously recorded au/à segmentation, but do not securely settle it. In the later parenthesis, the small oval followed by a shallow joined u course supports ou rather than a mathematical dot-minus operator. Fixant, both P labels and a_i are clear.'},
'B15':{'final':f['B15'].replace(*neg).replace('$), et','$) et'),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Remove the unshown comma after the closing parenthesis and broaden ne/un/en.','ink':'The closing parenthesis after a_j,a_k is followed by blank paper and et; there is no separate comma. The next short word has two compressed low courses, permitting ne, un or en. Passant is followed on the next baseline by the clear pas par a_i; pas is not omitted. The old short word has an A-like initial, so Au remains tentative. The inserted parenthesis reads pour1 membership Gamma and its guide joins before les, after the three l labels.'},
'B16':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain des and do not add low spots as punctuation.','ink':'After autour the article has a d loop, low e course and distinct terminal s hook. The two tiny spots below direct both lie beneath the normal text baseline, instead of straddling it like the written colon elsewhere. They do not establish a colon or semicolon in the phrase.'},
'B17':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain the qualified destination list.','ink':'All three destination labels are retraced: a-like loops join the0,1 and infinity forms. The two comma positions are clear. The grouped alternative already represents the same uncertain symbols as the independent reader’s separately qualified labels, without pretending to recover a rewriting sequence.'},
'B19':{'use_first':True,'adjudication':'Retain the prime/no-prime alternative.','ink':'The separate high tick is dark and lies between the index1 and the next l0. Its placement permits a prime on l1, but does not exclude an incidental pen trace. The label(1), separate vertical rule, outer factors and equality1 are clear.'},
'B20':{'final':f['B20'].replace(*mark),'changed':True,'adjudication':'Broaden the looped mark to a brace/question/parenthesis ambiguity.','ink':'After the clear exclamation mark there is a separate narrow sign with an upper loop, long descending middle and a lower fork/return. No detached question-mark dot is visible. Its overall contour is compatible with a closing brace, while an irregular question mark or parenthesis remains possible. On peut l’écrire and all three minus-one exponents are independently clear.'}}
for x in r['changes']:
 if x['id']=='s017-02':x.update(final=x['final'].replace(*slash),ink=c['B04']['ink'],crop='crops/second_145_scan017_B04.png',box=b['B04'])
 if x['id']=='s017-05':x.update(final=x['final'].replace(*left),ink=c['B07']['ink'],crop='crops/second_145_scan017_B07.png',box=b['B07'])
 if x['id']=='s017-14':x.update(final=x['final'].replace(*cross),ink=c['B12']['ink'],crop='crops/second_145_scan017_B12.png',box=b['B12'])
 if x['id']=='s017-20':x.update(final=x['final'].replace(*neg),ink=c['B15']['ink'],crop='crops/second_145_scan017_B15.png',box=b['B15'])
 if x['id']=='s017-30':x.update(final=x['final'].replace(*mark),ink=c['B20']['ink'],crop='crops/second_145_scan017_B20.png',box=b['B20'])
r['changes'].append({'id':'s017-32','place':'closing parenthesis after a_j,a_k, before et','C':'$a_j,a_k$), et','H':'$a_j,a_k$), et','final':'$a_j,a_k$) et','ink':c['B15']['ink'],'confidence':'high','kind':'text not on the page','c_changed':True,'h_changed':True,'marked_in_H':'no','crop':'crops/second_145_scan017_B15.png','box':b['B15'],'error_category':[9,10],'math_consequence':''})
